error[not_mutable]: `p` is lent read-only, the caller's own place, so it cannot be written — where the function changes it, take it `@p` in the signature and at every call site; where it changes a copy, bind one, `n @= p`
  at tests/golden/full/lent-is-named-where-an-at-parameter-only-reads.hero:25:22
     |
  25 |     return pt_value(@p)  #~ not_mutable
     |                      ^
  note: `pt_value` is a function of C: where its header only reads what this argument lends, through a pointer to `const`, declare that parameter `lent` with no `@` in its group and hand it `p` unmarked; a C function that writes it needs the caller's place, `@p`, in this function's signature too
